From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 23:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP: clean up stale MLD links after SA Query timeout

An authorized MLD station can reconnect without first sending a
deauthentication frame.  PMF requires hostapd to keep the old station and
keys alive while the SA Query is pending.  Once the query times out, however,
the association path currently keeps the authorized partner STA objects.
Creating the partner links for the new association then fails with "MLD:
link: Station already exists" and the station falls back to a single link.

Perform the destructive cleanup only after the SA Query timeout has been
confirmed.  Drop every reference to the shared WPA state machine before
freeing partner STA objects, and use ap_sta_re_add() to remove all partner
links and put the association-link STA back into the driver as an
unassociated peer.  This ordering makes the main peer available before the
new partner peers are installed.

Restore the userspace authentication flag cleared by ap_sta_re_add(), and
reset the propagated SA Query timeout immediately so a later association
attempt cannot repeat the cleanup and remove the freshly added main peer.
The MLD-AP check also covers an old MLD station reconnecting as a legacy
station, whose freshly parsed authentication state no longer has mld_sta set.

Based on Qualcomm's MLD STA reconnection and SA Query timeout fixes.

Patch-dependency: 991-AP-fix-legacy-station-roaming-between-MLD-links.patch

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11.c | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -7475,6 +7475,48 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 		goto fail;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/*
+	 * Authentication must not tear down an existing PMF association while
+	 * its SA Query is pending. Once the query has timed out, remove all old
+	 * MLD link objects before parsing and installing the new association.
+	 */
+	if ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) && sta->sa_query_timed_out &&
+	    hapd->conf->mld_ap) {
+		struct wpa_state_machine *sm = sta->wpa_sm;
+		bool authenticated = !!(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_AUTH);
+
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+			   "MLD: Re-add STA " MACSTR
+			   " after timed out SA Query procedure",
+			   MAC2STR(sta->addr));
+
+		/* All link STA objects share this state machine. Clear every
+		 * reference before ap_sta_re_add() frees the old partners. */
+		if (sm) {
+			clear_wpa_sm_for_each_partner_link(hapd, sta);
+			clear_wpa_sm_for_all_sta(hapd, sm);
+			wpa_auth_sta_deinit(sm);
+			sta->wpa_sm = NULL;
+		}
+
+		/* check_authorized=0 is intentional: SA Query has proved that
+		 * the old authorized association can now be replaced. Re-adding
+		 * the main peer before processing the MLE lets the driver accept
+		 * the new partner peers. */
+		if (ap_sta_re_add(hapd, sta, 0) < 0) {
+			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+				   "MLD: Failed to re-add STA after SA Query timeout");
+			resp = WLAN_STATUS_AP_UNABLE_TO_HANDLE_NEW_STA;
+			goto fail;
+		}
+
+		if (authenticated)
+			sta->flags |= WLAN_STA_AUTH;
+		ap_sta_set_sa_query_timeout(hapd, sta, 0);
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
 	/*
 	 * sta->capability is used in check_assoc_ies() for RRM enabled
 	 * capability element.
-- 
